      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to express the four positive integers in terms of their remainders when divided by 11. Let's denote the four integers by \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\). Given the remainders when these integers are divided by 11, we can write:\n\n\\[ a \\equiv 2 \\pmod{11} \\]\n\\[ b \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11} \\]\n\\[ c \\equiv 6 \\pmod{11} \\]\n\\[ d \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11} \\]\n\nThis means that the integers \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) can be written as:\n\n\\[ a = 11k + 2 \\]\n\\[ b = 11m + 4 \\]\n\\[ c = 11n + 6 \\]\n\\[ d = 11p + 8 \\]\n\nfor some integers \\(k\\), \\(m\\), \\(n\\), and \\(p\\).\n\nThe sum of these four integers is:\n\n\\[ a + b + c + d = (11k + 2) + (11m + 4) + (11n + 6) + (11p + 8) \\]\n\\[ = 11(k + m + n + p) + (2 + 4 + 6 + 8) \\]\n\\[ = 11(k + m + n + p) + 20 \\]\n\nWe need to find the remainder when this sum is divided by 11. Since \\(11(k + m + n + p)\\) is a multiple of 11, it leaves a remainder of 0 when divided by 11. Therefore, the remainder when \\(a + b + c + d\\) is divided by 11 is the same as the remainder when 20 is divided by 11.\n\nLet's calculate the remainder of 20 when divided by 11:\n\n\\[ 20 \\div 11 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 9 \\]\n\nSo the remainder is 9. Here is the Python code to verify this reasoning:\n\n```python\n# Given remainders\nremainders = [2, 4, 6, 8]\n\n# Calculate the sum of the remainders\nsum_of_remainders = sum(remainders)\n\n# Calculate the remainder when the sum is divided by 11\nfinal_remainder = sum_of_remainders % 11\n\nprint(final_remainder)\n```\n```output\n9\n```\nThe remainder when the sum of the four integers is divided by 11 is \\(\\boxed{9}\\).",
